      "writtenOn": "2026-09-14T13:51:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Without the separate status code, a client cannot distinguish \"no usable token currently exists\" from \"this endpoint is administratively disabled\".\n\n- `404 Not Found` remains the normal per-account state: no cached token, or no usable token after refresh. The user may be able to fix that by signing in again, or the administrator may need to fix the provider configuration.\n\n- `409 Conflict` means the Gerrit server configuration makes this endpoint unusable: `cache.oauth_tokens.memoryLimit \u003d 0` disables token storage, so Gerrit will drop tokens on login and re-authentication will not help. The operator must re-enable the cache, or clients must use a different credential flow.\n\nSo the client can report a configuration problem for 409 instead of misleading the user into another login loop.",
      "parentUuid": "3ec33a72_d989b110",
      "revId": "e1d85d244d4c5a552b934fb0738e9dc40a6005bd",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
